# skill_creator (project-local)

When creating a new skill in this repo, always produce **two files**:

1. `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` — canonical full version
2. `.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc` — thin pointer with frontmatter

The full procedure (naming conventions, frontmatter rules, when to add `globs`, templates, anti-patterns) is in [.claude/skills/skill_creator/SKILL.md](mdc:.claude/skills/skill_creator/SKILL.md).

Read that file when this rule triggers, then follow it.

**Quick rules:**

- Names: `snake_case`, English, lowercase, no spaces or hyphens
- `description:` in frontmatter must start with «Use this skill when...» and list concrete triggers
- `description` is identical between SKILL.md and .mdc
- `.mdc` references SKILL.md via `[link](mdc:.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md)` — never duplicate full content
- Add `globs:` to `.mdc` only when the skill reacts to file edits in a known location
- `alwaysApply: false` unless there's a strong reason
- Reference existing skills as style guides: `docs_lookup`, `docs_updater`, `release_notes_updater`
